; Find the exit that has the first object as its obstacle
;
; Loads the first object (#R$B6E8) and joins the exit walk of #R$9F2D with its
; field selector set to 1, the obstacle byte of the exit record. Used to find the
; exit a door, web or river blocks.
;
; O:A The obstacle id, $FF when the actor's location has no such exit
; O:IX The exit record (direction, obstacle, destination) found
@label=FindExitByObstacle
c$9F25 LD A,($B6E8)
*$9F28 PUSH AF
 $9F29 LD A,$01         ; 1 = field +1 (the obstacle), stored by #R$9F30 into the displacement at #R$9F42
 $9F2B JR $9F30
